B1 · Live disruption map (dio.html)
  - New w-12 widget above Territory Pulse
  - Leaflet 1.9.4 tile map (OpenStreetMap), territory-zoomed per DIO
    (Emma UK / Françoise FR / Sofia ES / other → central Europe)
  - 17 seeded disruption events across 8 kinds: weather, notams,
    atfm, strike, wildfire, disaster, volcanic, incidents
  - Per-kind filter chips with total-count badges; toggle to show/hide
    each kind's layer live on the map
  - Per-marker click-popup showing kind, title, meta line, timestamp
  - Coloured circle markers matching chip colours
  - initDisruptionMap fires 60ms after render() completes; defensive
    try/catch so a Leaflet load failure never breaks the page

B2 · Eurocontrol portal + storage-destination framing (evidence-atfm.html)
  - New prominent callout at page top: 'Open live portal →' button
    linking to public.nm.eurocontrol.int
  - Reframed page copy so it's clear the two panels below are
    DefendAble's own storage of what we've pulled, not the source
  - Panel h3s now say 'our snapshot' / 'our archive' with a note
    directing users to the live portal for authoritative view
  - Page-sub reworded: 'Storage destination for everything DefendAble
    has pulled from Eurocontrol NM public NOP + CODA retrospective'

Cache-bust: s11a across the two touched HTMLs.
